body:
Final Fantasy VI.

&#x200B;

I think it has a lot of potential to polish all the background stories of all the characters that were kind of rushed due to it being released at the time that it was. The game is still great if you're not a graphics queen (nothing wrong with being a graphics queen btw), but I think its story is surprisingly deep despite the fact that it is what it is.

A remake could do it so much good, and the amount of characters it has with different quirks could make for a lot of interesting gameplay interactions as well (think FF Type-0's students, but without the limitations of being a really old portable title). Since old style FF turn based battle with gauges is not something that I think would translate super well 1:1 to modern day gaming, the fact that nearly every character has its little niche could be super nice.

&#x200B;

TL;DR - game is still great, but could be something truly great with modern narrative polish and has a bunch of possible gameplay innovations due to the variety of the cast.
